Report SLANG_UNKNOWN_SIZE for the element count of an array whose length is not a constant.

spReflectionType_GetSpecializedElementCount (source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp), which
spReflectionType_GetElementCount and TypeReflection::getElementCount forward to, ends with:

    return isUnsized                       ? 0
           : elementCount->isLinkTimeVal() ? SLANG_UNKNOWN_SIZE
                                           : (size_t)getIntVal(elementCount);       // 653-655

An array sized by a specialization constant ([vk::constant_id(0)] const int kCount) has a
DeclRefIntVal length that is not a link-time value (DeclRefIntVal::_isLinkTimeValOverride checks
for extern), and tryFoldIntVal does not fold it, so getIntVal is reached, and getIntVal of anything
but a ConstantIntVal is SLANG_UNEXPECTED (source/slang/slang-syntax.cpp:898-905). The resulting
Slang::InternalError leaves the extern "C" function: a structured exception on Windows, a call to
std::terminate on Linux and macOS. slangc -reflection-json stops the same way on such a shader.
slang.h:2633-2638 documents SLANG_UNKNOWN_SIZE for exactly this case, and the size and offset
queries on the same array already return it.

This returns the value of a ConstantIntVal and SLANG_UNKNOWN_SIZE for any other length, the answer
already given for a link-time constant. Every count that was returned before is returned unchanged;
only the lengths that threw now report SLANG_UNKNOWN_SIZE. A regression test is added as
tools/slang-unit-test/unit-test-specialization-sized-array-reflection.cpp.

Measured on v2026.21 with struct SeBlock { float4 seItems[kSeCount]; float seTail; }: before,
both calls end the process (win-x64: the exception surfaces as a structured exception); after,
both return 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFE (win-x64, linux-x64).
diff --git a/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp b/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp
index 35e27abad..3f7940272 100644
--- a/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp
+++ b/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp
@@ -650,9 +650,16 @@ SLANG_API size_t spReflectionType_GetSpecializedElementCount(
         }
     }
 
-    return isUnsized                       ? 0
-           : elementCount->isLinkTimeVal() ? SLANG_UNKNOWN_SIZE
-                                           : (size_t)getIntVal(elementCount);
+    if (isUnsized)
+        return 0;
+
+    // An element count that is not a constant, such as a link-time constant or a
+    // specialization constant, is not known until the program is linked or specialized.
+    //
+    if (auto constantElementCount = as<ConstantIntVal>(elementCount))
+        return (size_t)constantElementCount->getValue();
+
+    return SLANG_UNKNOWN_SIZE;
 }
 
 SLANG_API SlangReflectionType* spReflectionType_GetElementType(SlangReflectionType* inType)
